  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\n\nWarm advection returns for most of the Central Plains areas \nWednesday as the H8 high pushes off to the east. This may help force \nsome scattered showers (30-50%) Wednesday morning, particularly over \nnortheast Nebraska. By then, the H5 pattern shows predominately \nsouthwest flow in our area as ridging takes place over the southern \nCONUS. This should allow for continued shortwave trofs to ride said \nflow, and when paired with the H8 warm advection, will see more \nchances for showers and some storms. Thursday, early Friday, and \nearly Saturday appear to have the best chances (50-70%) at us seeing \nwetting precip areawide. Chances somewhat decrease by Sunday but \nwith several subtleties noted per model guidance at that point. \n\nTemperatures remain in the cool side through Friday with highs in \nthe 60s. There is some indication we warm up to the low to mid \n70s though toward the tail end of the long term period as some \nH5 ridging builds over most of the central and southern CONUS.",
